  "worked_solution": "The cardinality of a finite set $X$ is the number of elements in $X.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $X:$\n\n$$\n{3}^{2},\\,{5}^{2},\\,{7}^{2},\\,{9}^{2}\n$$\n\nSince $X$ has $4$ elements, its cardinality is $|X|=4.$",
